{% set actor_tags_enabled = is_audio_tags_enabled(npc.UUID) %}
{% set narrator_tags_enabled = is_audio_tags_enabled(get_narrator_uuid()) and is_narration_enabled() %}
{% set dialogue_mode = render_mode == "full" or render_mode == "transform" %}
{% set thought_mode = render_mode == "thoughts" %}
{% set has_audio_tags = actor_tags_enabled or narrator_tags_enabled %}

{% if has_audio_tags and (dialogue_mode or thought_mode) %}
  {% set tts_engine = get_actor_tts(npc.UUID) %}
  {% set useHiggsV3Tags = (tts_engine == "higgs" or tts_engine == "higgs_v3") and actor_tags_enabled %}
  {% set useChatterboxTags = tts_engine == "chatterbox" and actor_tags_enabled %}

  {% set chatterboxEmotionTags = ["[angry]", "[fear]", "[surprised]", "[whispering]", "[advertisement]", "[dramatic]", "[narration]","[happy]", "[sarcastic]"] %}
  {% set chatterboxSoundTags = ["[clear throat]","[sigh]","[shush]","[cough]","[groan]","[sniff]","[gasp]","[chuckle]","[laugh]","[crying]"] %}
  ## Voice Performance Tags
  {% if useHiggsV3Tags %}
  Use control tags `<|category:tag|>` to steer emotion, prosody, style, and sound effects.
  {% else %}
  Use [square bracket tags] to direct vocal performance. Tags control emotion, delivery, and reactions—the AI voice interprets them contextually.
  {% endif %}
  
  {% if useHiggsV3Tags %}
    {% set exampleTag1 = "<|sfx:sigh|>Haah," %}
    {% set exampleTag2 = "<|emotion:elation|>" %}
    {% set exampleTag3 = "<|style:whispering|>" %}
    {% set exampleTag4 = "<|prosody:expressive_high|>" %}

    **Format:** `<|category:tag|>`. Only use tags from the catalog below — anything else degrades audio or gets read aloud literally.

    **Placement rules:**
    - **Sentence-level** (emotion, style, `speed_*`, `pitch_*`, `expressive_*`): put at the **very start** of the sentence, glued directly to the first word — no space. Colors the whole sentence.
      e.g. `<|emotion:elation|>Welcome aboard!`
    - **Inline sfx**: insert at the exact spot the sound occurs. Glue the tag (no space) to a short onomatopoeia, then continue the line.
      e.g. `<|sfx:cough|>Ahem, let's begin.`
    - **Pauses:** Prefer plain `...` in the text for a natural short pause — it works more reliably than the pause tag. Use `<|prosody:long_pause|>` only for a longer, deliberate dramatic hold.
      e.g. `Hello there... and welcome to the show.`

    **Stacking:** You may combine **one tag per category** at the start of a sentence — e.g. emotion + style, or emotion + a sentence-level prosody tag — since they control different things (feeling vs. vocal technique vs. delivery mechanics). Inline `sfx` can be added anywhere on top of that.
    Do **not** stack two tags from the *same* category (e.g. two emotions, or `pitch_low` + `pitch_high`) — pick the one that best fits the moment.
    - ✅ `<|emotion:arousal|><|style:whispering|>Come closer... I need you.`
    - ✅ `<|emotion:surprise|><|prosody:expressive_high|>I can't believe you! <|sfx:laughter|> HaHaHa!`
    - ✅ `<|emotion:elation|><|sfx:laughter|>Haha, welcome, welcome!`
    - ❌ `<|emotion:anger|><|emotion:disgust|>How dare you.` (two emotions)

    **You don't need a tag to use a vocal sound.** Plain onomatopoeia — "Haha", "Mmh", "Ugh", "Aah", "Sff" — can appear directly in the line with no `<|sfx:...|>` tag, as light natural texture. Use the actual `sfx` tag when you want it rendered as a distinct, emphasized performance beat instead.

    **Tag catalog (43 total):**
    - Emotion — `affection, amusement, anger, arousal, awe, bitterness, confusion, contemplation, contentment, determination, disgust, elation, enthusiasm, fear, helplessness, longing, pride, relief, sadness, shame, surprise`
    - Style — `singing, shouting, whispering`
    - Prosody (sentence-level) — `speed_very_slow, speed_slow, speed_fast, speed_very_fast, pitch_low, pitch_high, expressive_high, expressive_low`
    - Prosody (inline) — `long_pause` (for `pause`, prefer `...` instead — see above)
    - SFX (inline, glued to onomatopoeia) — `cough, laughter, crying, screaming, burping, humming, sigh, sniff, sneeze`

    **Examples:**
    - `<|emotion:elation|>Welcome aboard, we are absolutely thrilled to have you here!`
    - `<|emotion:arousal|><|style:whispering|>Come closer, I have a little secret to share.`
    - `<|sfx:laughter|>Haha, so glad you could make it!`
    - `<|emotion:elation|><|sfx:laughter|>Haha, welcome, welcome, we're so happy you're here!`
    - `Hello there... and welcome to the show.`
    - `Mmh, that smells wonderful.` *(plain onomatopoeia, no tag needed)*
  {% elif useChatterboxTags %}
    {% set exampleTag1 = "[sigh]" %}
    {% set exampleTag2 = "[happy]" %}
    {% set exampleTag3 = "[whispering]" %}
    {% set exampleTag4 = "[dramatic]" %}
    **Allowed emotion tags (OPTIONAL, at the beginning of emotional sentence):**
    {{join(chatterboxEmotionTags, ", ")}}
    **Allowed sound tags (OPTIONAL, may appear ANYWHERE):**
    {{ join(chatterboxSoundTags, ", ") }}
    **How to write each dialogue/thought line**
    - You MAY start the line with ONE emotion tag, but it is optional.
    - You MAY insert multiple sound tags anywhere in the line (start, middle, end).
    - Sound tags must be standalone tokens (surrounded by spaces or punctuation), not attached to words.
    - Do NOT invent other bracketed text. Only use the allowed tags above.
    - Keep tags meaningful; don’t spam them (typically 0–3 sound tags per line unless the scene demands it).
    
    **Examples**
    - [whispering] Keep your voice down - [shush] - they’ll hear us. [sigh]
    - I told you not to touch that - [groan] - ever again. [cough]
    - [happy] [clear throat] So… we agree? [chuckle] Great.
  {% else %}
    {% set exampleTag1 = "[sighs]" %}
    {% set exampleTag2 = "[excited]" %}
    {% set exampleTag3 = "[softly]" %}
    {% set exampleTag4 = "[dramatic tone]" %}
    **Tag types:** emotions ([sad], [excited]), delivery ([whispers], [shouts], [slowly]), reactions ([sighs], [laughs], [clears throat]), pacing ([pause], [dramatic tone])
  {% endif %}
  {% if actor_tags_enabled %}
    **Dialogue{% if thought_mode %}/thoughts{% endif %}:** {{exampleTag1}} I suppose you're right. / Did you see that? {{exampleTag2}} Incredible!
  {% endif %}
  {% if narrator_tags_enabled %}
    **Narration:** *{{exampleTag3}} {{ decnpc(npc.UUID).name }} turns away.* / *{{exampleTag4}} The room falls silent.*
  {% endif %}
  {% if not actor_tags_enabled and narrator_tags_enabled %}
    Tags only work in *narration*, not dialogue.
  {% endif %}
  {% if actor_tags_enabled and not narrator_tags_enabled and is_narration_enabled() %}
    Tags only work in dialogue, not *narration*.
  {% endif %}

  {% if not useChatterboxTags and not useHiggsV3Tags %}
    Use sparingly—1-2 per response max.
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}

